SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:museum,science,family,all_audiences
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Field Museum - Events\\nCost: Included with admissi
 on\\nAges: All ages\\nCategory: General\\n\\nEach year\, Indigenous People
 s’ Day is an opportunity to recognize and honor the cultures\, tradition
 s\, and ongoing contributions of Indigenous communities. It is also a mome
 nt to reflect on the histories that shape our world today and to celebrate
  the resilience of Indigenous peoples across the Americas and beyond. We i
 nvite you to join us in honoring Indigenous traditions\, cultures\, and li
 ves—and in recognizing the deep and ongoing connections between Indigeno
 us peoples and the lands we share.\\n\\nMore info: https://www.fieldmuseum
 .org/our-events/indigenous-peoples-day/indigenous-peoples-day
LOCATION:Field Museum\, 1400 S Lake Shore Dr\, Chicago\, IL 60605
URL:https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/indigenous-peoples-day/indigeno
 us-peoples-day
