SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:museum,science,family,museum_professional,community_scientist,r
 esearcher,adults
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Field Museum - Events\\nAges: All ages\\nCategory: 
 Arts & Crafts\\n\\nJoin us for a talk by Pavitra Muralidhar from the Unive
 rsity of Chicago. This session will take place in Ward Hall on the lower l
 evel. If coming from outside the Museum\, please enter through the west do
 ors. Reach out to sruane@fieldmuseum.org with any questions. The A. Watson
  Armour III Seminar Series is a weekly seminar highlighting the research o
 f science professionals across a broad spectrum of scientific interests\, 
 disciplines\, and lived experiences. This series connects the Field Museum
 ’s research\, collections\, conservation\, and associated community with
  professionals at the forefront of life\, geophysical\, and social science
 s. Lectures are open to the public and regularly highlight or complement r
 esearch conducted by Field Museum staff and affiliates. Have a speaker to 
 suggest? Contact us at armourseminars@fieldmuseum.org.\\n\\nMore info: htt
 ps://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/a-watson-armour-iii-research-seminar-s
 eries/armour-seminar-pavitra-muralidhar
LOCATION:Field Museum\, 1400 S Lake Shore Dr\, Chicago\, IL 60605
URL:https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/a-watson-armour-iii-research-se
 minar-series/armour-seminar-pavitra-muralidhar
