SUMMARY:Talk Story: Pacific and Filipino Voices in the Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261027T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261027T131500
DTSTAMP:20261009T150201Z
UID:7c914853d714c14d67226c59cf7b3c7f@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:museum,science,family,all_audiences
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Field Museum - Events\\nCost: Included with admissi
 on\\nAges: All ages\\nCategory: General\\n\\nJoin the Field Museum for Tal
 k Story: Pacific and Filipino Voices in the Museum \, a conversation with 
 Field Museum staff and Filipino American community partners about the impo
 rtance of collaboration\, shared knowledge\, and community voices in museu
 m work. Drawing from partnerships connected to the Museum’s Pacific and 
 Filipino collections\, panelists will explore what collaboration looks lik
 e in practice—from collections care and interpretation to education and 
 community engagement—and how these relationships can create new opportun
 ities for people to connect with their histories and heritage. The convers
 ation will also reflect on lessons learned\, unexpected discoveries\, and 
 how museums can continue building trust and creating meaningful ways for c
 ommunities to engage with collections. This event will take place in Ward 
 Hall on the lower level and is part of our celebration of Filipino America
 n Heritage Month .\\n\\nMore info: https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/
 cultural-programming/talk-story-pacific-and-filipino-voices-in-the-museum
LOCATION:Field Museum\, 1400 S Lake Shore Dr\, Chicago\, IL 60605
URL:https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/cultural-programming/talk-story
 -pacific-and-filipino-voices-in-the-museum
