UID:1f35bd5d7a23ed1d963718067affb8d1@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:museum,science,family,all_audiences
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Field Museum - Events\\nCost: Included with admissi
 on\\nAges: All ages\\nCategory: General\\n\\nCelebrate Bat Week at the Fie
 ld Museum!  Meet Beatriz Dybas da Natividade and Dr Amanda Grunwald\, and
  hear about their field seasons in the Dominican Republic and Peru\, while
  you examine bat specimens and learn about their diversity in the Neotropi
 cs. Discover why bats are not something to be feared\, but are instead am
 azing creatures vital to the health of the natural world and economy. Pres
 ented by Beatriz Dybas da Natividade\, PhD candidate at the University of
  Illinois at Chicago\, and Dr Amanda Grunwald\, Post-doc researcher at the
  Field Museum.\\n\\nMore info: https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/meet
 -a-scientist/meet-a-scientist-neotropical-bats
LOCATION:Field Museum\, 1400 S Lake Shore Dr\, Chicago\, IL 60605
URL:https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/meet-a-scientist/meet-a-scienti
 st-neotropical-bats
